# NIP-05 identity — serve static nostr.json before SPA fallback
/.well-known/*  /.well-known/:splat  200

# Product metrics: CF Pages Function functions/metrics.json.js proxies
# /metrics.json → api.satohash.io (dist static copy is stripped at build).
# Do NOT add a /metrics.json redirect here.
# Canonical SoT for HQ: https://api.satohash.io/metrics.json
#
# NOTE: Do NOT add /assets/* or /b/* → 404 rewrites. On satohash.io apex CF has
# cached SPA fallback HTML under asset URLs (System Desync / Unexpected token '<').
# Bundles use /b/*; stale recovery is PWA cleanup + ErrorBoundary hard reset.

# Thank-you pages — real static pages (200, not the SPA shell) so donors/leads
# never bounce to the homepage or a dead end. Served before the SPA catch-all.
/thank-you      /thank-you.html   200
/thanks         /thank-you.html   200
/thankyou       /thank-you.html   200
/success        /thank-you.html   200
/donate/thank-you /thank-you.html 200

# SPA fallback — BrowserRouter requires all routes to serve index.html
# Static files at the site root (incl. Google Search Console HTML) are served first.
/*    /index.html   200
